# LidarLouderPing: the texts of its Tuning slider, in English. Godot shows English for any language without its own
# file (its fallback locale), so another language only needs a copy of this file with its Language and msgstr lines
# translated, loaded in ModMain.gd.
msgid ""
msgstr ""
"Language: en\n"
"Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8\n"

msgid "TUNE_LIDARLOUDERPING_GAIN"
msgstr "Audible feedback boost"

msgid "TUNE_LIDARLOUDERPING_GAIN_DESC"
msgstr ""
"LidarLouderPing mod: how much louder the ping for sensor contacts plays, on top of the game's own volume. Only "
"applies while \"Audible feedback for sensor contacts\" is on. About every 10 dB sounds twice as loud; 0 dB leaves "
"the game's volume. With a large boost, the game holds the pings back and briefly lowers other sounds along with "
"them. While this setting is selected, the preview plays pings from a far, a halfway and a close contact."
